        "original_id": "f520cf1b-7581-5d06-8feb-2238ee10357e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beatrice Tinsley, Brian Tinsley\n- Organizations: American Astronomical Society, Southwest Center for Advanced Studies, University of Texas at Dallas\n- Awards: Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize\n- Roles: astronomer, cosmologist\n- Topics: galaxy evolution, astronomy, astrophysics\n\nFacts:\n- Beatrice Muriel Hill Tinsley was born on 27 January 1941 and died on 23 March 1981.\n- Beatrice Tinsley was a British-born New Zealand astronomer and cosmologist.\n- Beatrice Tinsley made fundamental research contributions to understanding how galaxies evolve, grow, and die.\n- Brian Tinsley and his wife Beatrice Tinsley came to Dallas to work at the newly formed Southwest Center for Advanced Studies.\n- The Southwest Center for Advanced Studies became the University of Texas at Dallas in 1969.\n- The American Astronomical Society awards the Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize every other year.\n- The Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize recognizes an outstanding research contribution to astronomy or astrophysics of an exceptionally creative or innovative character.\n- The Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize is named in honor of the cosmologist and astronomer Beatrice Tinsley.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
